# Classes under one parent, one row per class, parent and kind (owl:Class or rdfs:Class), so the report can compare what siblings of one kind say (their properties and their rules): two siblings that say the same are perhaps one class. One row per class, never per pair: a parent with 200 children is 200 rows here, and was 19,900 pairs that rdflib could not finish in 30 seconds.
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
PREFIX dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>
PREFIX dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/>
PREFIX sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#>
PREFIX ss: <urn:semantic-studio:check:>
SELECT DISTINCT ?iri ?type ?parent WHERE {
  VALUES ?type { owl:Class rdfs:Class }
  ?iri a ?type ; rdfs:subClassOf ?parent .
  FILTER(isIRI(?iri) && isIRI(?parent) && ss:own(?iri))
}
ORDER BY ?parent ?type ?iri
